  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 255 AM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nCooler/less hot weather arrives on Saturday with more appreciable\ncold air advection in the wake of the cold front. However, the \nstrongest cold air advection will remain to our northeast across \nthe Great Lakes and Midwest. As a result, the most significant \ncool down will be across north central Oklahoma. High temperatures\nare forecast to range from the near 90 deg F (north central \nOklahoma) to near 100 deg F (southwest Oklahoma and western north \nTexas). In other words, this cold front will bring us closer to \nnormal for early August. \n\nNear normal temperatures will continue into Sunday before a slow \nwarming trend begins on Monday with a strengthening ridge aloft \nand attendant thermal ridge expanding eastward--back toward the \nSouthern Plains.\n\nMahale",
